note.text:
A town is a large settlement where most people work in industry, trade and services rather than farming.
Urban landscape (what a town looks like):
• the central business district (CBD): offices, banks, big shops, ministries, tall buildings (Akwa in Douala, the centre of Yaoundé);
• residential areas: rich planned quarters with villas (Bastos, Bonapriso) and poor, crowded, unplanned quarters (shanty towns, slums) with houses of planks and zinc;
• industrial zones (Bassa in Douala), markets, the port, the airport, roads and roundabouts.
Informal activities are small jobs not registered with the State and paying little or no tax: street hawking, bayam-sellam (food retailers), bike and motorbike taxis (benskin), shoe repair, call-boxes and phone repair, roadside food.
